<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4921" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">baptistērĭum</span></b> ,
		ii, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαπτιστήριον</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A place for bathing</i> or <i>swimming</i>, <i>a vessel for bathing</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep.
				5, 6, 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2,
				17, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 2,
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			eccl. Lat., <i>a baptistery</i>, <i>a
				baptismal font</i>, <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 4,
			15</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
